==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|gob-rope|gaub rope|gaub-rope|gab rope|gab-rope|gog rope|gog-rope}}
* {{alt|en|gob line|gob-line|gaub line|gaub-line|gab line|gab-line|gog line|gog-line}}

===Etymology===
{{unknown|en}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|nautical}} A [[rope]] or [[chain]] [[run]]{{mdash}}[[usually]] in [[pair]]s{{mdash}}from the [[martingale]] or [[dolphin striker]] to the [[side]]s of the [[bow]]s and [[use]]d to [[stay]] the [[jib boom]] and [[flying jib boom]]. {{defdate|1841}}
#*: In order to avoid [[girt]]ing the [[tug]], it is normal practice to employ a {{'}}'''gob rope'''{{'}} (sometimes referred to as a gog rope). It is generally used at the [[aft]] end of the tug's deck to change the towing position ([[fulcrum]] point) from the [[amidships]] position to a position right aft. This effectively generates a turning motion as opposed to a [[capsize]] motion, causing a [[slew]]ing action on the tug.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|stay}}, {{l|en|backrope}}, {{l|en|back-rope}}, {{l|en|back rope}}, {{l|en|martingale backrope}}, &c.

